---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import { offers } from '@config/site';
---
<Base
  title="Competitive Radar"
  description="Ongoing competitive intelligence for pricing changes, product launches, positioning shifts, funding, integrations and emerging rivals."
  path="/market-intelligence/"
>
  <section class="rad13-hero" data-surface="dark">
    <div class="container rad13-hero__inner">
      <span class="label">COMPETITIVE RADAR</span>
      <h1>Know when the competitive picture changes.</h1>
      <p>A point-in-time brief answers a question now. Competitive Radar is the ongoing layer for teams that need important competitor moves surfaced and verified before the information goes stale.</p>
      <div class="rad13-actions"><a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=radar">Ask About Ongoing Intelligence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/method/">See the evidence standard →</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container rad13-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="label">ONGOING, NOT AUTOMATIC NOISE</span>
          <h2>Monitor the moves that can change a decision.</h2>
          <p class="rad13-lede">Radar is not a promise to dump every competitor mention into a dashboard. The objective is to identify changes that matter, verify the source, and preserve the boundary between observed fact and analytical interpretation.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rad13-panel"><small class="mono">ENGAGEMENT</small><strong>{offers.radar.priceDisplay}</strong><p>{offers.radar.priceNote}.</p><small class="mono">CADENCE</small><b>{offers.radar.delivery}</b></aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section rad13-muted">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">WHAT CAN BE MONITORED</span>
        <div class="rad13-cards">
          <article><b>01</b><h3>Pricing</h3><p>Plan changes, packaging shifts, discount structures and public enterprise pricing signals.</p></article>
          <article><b>02</b><h3>Product</h3><p>Launches, changelog moves, integrations, model coverage and capability expansion.</p></article>
          <article><b>03</b><h3>Positioning</h3><p>Homepage, category, comparison and claim changes that signal a strategic shift.</p></article>
          <article><b>04</b><h3>Company moves</h3><p>Funding, expansion, leadership changes and other public signals relevant to competitive capacity.</p></article>
          <article><b>05</b><h3>Emerging rivals</h3><p>New companies entering the competitive set or moving close enough to deserve validation.</p></article>
          <article><b>06</b><h3>Decision alerts</h3><p>Verified changes framed around why they may matter rather than forwarded as unfiltered news.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container rad13-grid">
        <div><span class="label">SCOPE</span><h2>Built around the signals your team cannot afford to miss.</h2><p class="rad13-lede">Radar is scoped individually because the competitor set, signal types, cadence and decision context vary by company. The engagement begins by defining what deserves monitoring, how often the evidence should be reviewed and what threshold should trigger an alert.</p></div>
        <div class="rad13-rule"><b>OBSERVE</b><span>→</span><b>VERIFY</b><span>→</span><b>CLASSIFY</b><span>→</span><strong>SURFACE WHAT MATTERS</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section rad13-final" data-surface="dark">
      <div class="container"><span class="label">KEEP THE VIEW CURRENT</span><h2>Tell us what needs watching.</h2><p>We will scope the competitor set, signals and cadence around the decisions your team cannot afford to make on stale information.</p><a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=radar">Ask About Ongoing Intelligence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .rad13-hero{padding:clamp(5rem,10vw,8rem) 0;background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff}.rad13-hero__inner{max-width:70rem}.rad13-hero h1{max-width:13ch;margin:.8rem 0 1rem;font-size:clamp(3rem,7vw,6.2rem);line-height:.94;letter-spacing:-.055em}.rad13-hero p{max-width:53rem;color:#cbd8e8;font-size:1.18rem;line-height:1.7}.rad13-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:1rem;margin-top:1.7rem}.rad13-actions>a:not(.btn){font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:750;text-decoration:none;color:#dbe8ff}.rad13-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.25fr) minmax(16rem,.75fr);gap:clamp(2rem,7vw,6rem);align-items:start}.rad13-grid h2,.rad13-final h2{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,4.5vw,4.2rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:.6rem 0 1rem}.rad13-lede{font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--text-muted)}.rad13-panel{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--surface-border);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--bg-raised);display:grid;gap:.45rem}.rad13-panel strong{font:800 2rem/1 var(--font-display)}.rad13-panel small{color:var(--text-faint);letter-spacing:.08em;margin-top:.65rem}.rad13-panel p{margin:0;color:var(--text-muted)}.rad13-muted{background:var(--bg-raised)}.rad13-cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem;margin-top:1.4rem}.rad13-cards article{padding:1.35rem;border:1px solid var(--surface-border);border-radius:.85rem;background:var(--bg)}.rad13-cards b{font-family:var(--font-mono);color:var(--accent);font-size:.72rem}.rad13-cards h3{margin:.6rem 0 .45rem}.rad13-cards p{margin:0;color:var(--text-muted);line-height:1.6}.rad13-rule{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto auto auto auto auto auto auto;align-items:center;gap:.65rem;padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--surface-border);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--bg-raised);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.78rem}.rad13-rule span{color:var(--text-faint)}.rad13-rule strong{color:var(--accent)}.rad13-final{background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff}.rad13-final p{color:#cbd8e8;max-width:48rem;margin-bottom:1.4rem}@media(max-width:820px){.rad13-grid,.rad13-cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.rad13-rule{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
